        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs: document local text worker pattern",
        "body": "Closes #51333\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a docs gap where users mixing hosted and local models had to infer the cloud-orchestrator plus local-text-workers pattern from several separate pages.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a focused Gateway docs page that frames hosted models as the tool-using orchestrator and local models as bounded text workers for drafting, summarizing, rewriting, or JSON-only tasks. The page composes existing local model, CLI backend, sub-agent, llm-task, timeout, and sandbox guidance without changing runtime behavior or adding config.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can now find one recommended pattern for using local models safely as text-in/text-out workers while keeping tool use, approvals, and final decisions with a reliable orchestrator model.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: the new docs page is registered, parses as MDX, has valid internal links, and the new page title / related-link labels have zh-CN glossary entries.\n- Head SHA: 2b7cabc4bd0446f24ff0b5ae5c7c55b30642db41\n- Commands / artifacts:\n  - `git diff --check`\n  - `node scripts/docs-list.js | Select-String -Pattern \"local-text-workers|Local text workers\"`\n  - `node scripts/check-docs-mdx.mjs docs README.md`\n  - `node scripts/docs-link-audit.mjs`\n  - `node scripts/check-docs-i18n-glossary.mjs --base origin/main --head HEAD`\n  - GitHub current-head checks on 2b7cabc4bd0446f24ff0b5ae5c7c55b30642db41: `dependency-guard`, `security-sensitive-guard`, `Real behavior proof`, `auto-response`, `label`, Socket PR alerts, and Socket project report all passed.\n- Observed result:\n  - docs list includes `gateway\\local-text-workers.md`.\n  - MDX passed for 692 files.\n  - link audit reported `broken_links=0`.\n  - i18n glossary check passed with no missing-term output after adding `Local text workers`, `Local models`, `CLI backends`, `LLM task`, and `Multi-agent sandbox tools` glossary entries.\n  - `git diff --check` passed.\n- Not tested / proof gaps:\n  - No live Mintlify browser render captured.\n  - No runtime behavior changed.",
